// AutomationML Edition 2.1 (CAEX 3.0): the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// A CAEX file describing assembly cell AC-1 of a fictional plant builder, exchanged between its plant engineering and
// control engineering tools: an instance hierarchy of a work cell holding a welding robot with a vacuum gripper, a
// belt conveyor and a PLC, their ports and signal interfaces, the internal links between them, and attributes with
// units, semantics and nominal constraints. Behind the instances stand a system unit class library with the robot and
// gripper types — the gripper's supported role class mapped to a user-defined role class by attribute name — and
// user-defined role and interface class libraries, alongside external references to AutomationML's standard
// libraries.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

